      {
        "id": 88843,
        "name": "Envisioner",
        "username": "Envisioner",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-13T06:37:45.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Matchstickman\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/matchstickman/48/1880_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Matchstickman:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Why would Zhu Long raise his nemesis? How does his nemesis being <s>alive</s> around to interfere benefit him?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>He might enjoy the challenge of having a worthy adversary.&nbsp; He might believe Fixer can be converted to his way of thinking.&nbsp; He might be a seven-thousand-year-old immortal who is honor-bound to repay a favor that Fixer's great-great-great-to-the-umpteenth-grandfather did him in back in predynastic Egypt when they were both slaves of the Forgotten Pharaoh, and thus protects Fixer's life even while arranging for him to be out of the way of his schemes.&nbsp; There are any number of possible explanations.</p>",
