      {
        "id": 88844,
        "name": "TheSoundOfTrees",
        "username": "TheSoundOfTrees",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/da6949/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-13T08:30:23.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Matchstickman\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/matchstickman/48/1880_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Matchstickman:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Why would Zhu Long raise his nemesis? How does his nemesis being <s>alive</s> around to interfere benefit him?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Maybe Zhu Long is just the \"bad\" dragon, the one who brings evil ones back to life, and there is a \"good\" dragon somewhere who brought back Mr Fixer.</p>\n<p>Or maybe Zhu Long discovered a new very powerful mystic menace, something so dangerous for him and his plans that he decided to bring back his old powerful ennemy to fight it. Leading to the creation of the Dark Watch.</p>\n<p>Or Nightmist used powerful spells to force Zhu Long to bring back Fixer (or to ressurect him herself). Or negociated with him.</p>\n<p>Or Zhu Long was trying to resurect someone else, but Setback made him fumble and Mr FIxer was back instead <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n<p>Or…</p>",
        "post_number": 73,
